  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The **Fibonacci numbers**, commonly denoted `F(n)` form a sequence, called the **Fibonacci sequence**, such that each number is the sum of the two preceding ones, starting from `0` and `1`. That is,\n\n```\nF(0) = 0, F(1) = 1\nF(n) = F(n - 1) + F(n - 2), for n > 1.\n```\n\nWith `n`, calculate `F(n)`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 2\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: F(2) = F(1) + F(0) = 1 + 0 = 1.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 3\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: F(3) = F(2) + F(1) = 1 + 1 = 2.\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 4\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: F(4) = F(3) + F(2) = 2 + 1 = 3.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `0 <= n <= 30`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
